namespace DocuHelper.Agents
{
    public static partial class ClaudePrompt
    {
        internal const string WordRules = """
            Read first: read_paragraphs gives text, paragraph ids and (detail=format) character formatting, and find returns the character offsets edit_text and format_text accept; read_document shows what surrounds the text (comments, tracked changes, notes, objects, headings, page setup, headers and footers, styles, statistics) and its page numbers are estimates. Offsets count what read_paragraphs shows, so prefer match plus occurrence over counting characters.
            Edit text with edit_text (typing-like insert, delete, replace, split, join, paste) or replace_text (a phrase everywhere); use replace_paragraph only to rewrite a whole paragraph. A field's visible result is ordinary text: overwriting it replaces the field with plain text, and edits that would cut inside a field are refused. With revision tracking on, text edits are recorded as tracked changes but formatting changes are not.
            format_text changes characters (font, size, bold, italic, underline, color, highlight, case) on offsets or a match; format_paragraph handles alignment, styles, indents and spacing for one or several paragraphs; set_list makes bullets and numbers (never type the marks); edit_style and set_document_design change a style, the theme, fonts and colours for the whole document.
            edit_table works on the table id from read_paragraphs or insert_table (the id stays the same after every edit); rows and columns are 1-based and include the header row. Insert or delete rows and columns first, then merge or split, then set_widths and format (colours as #RRGGBB); use set_table_cell for text.
            set_page_setup changes the whole document by default (size, orientation, margins, columns, line numbers, vertical alignment, page borders, page color); scope section needs a paragraph id inside that section, and from_here starts a new section at the given paragraph. Orientation only swaps width and height; margins stay as they are.
            set_header_footer: pick part (header or footer), write preset or text or left/center/right with the tokens {page}, {pages}, {date}, {time}, {file}, {title}, {author}; page_number places a live number, format and start_at restyle or restart numbering; first-page and odd/even variants switch their flags on by themselves; later sections inherit the previous header unless given section=N. insert_page inserts page, column, line and section breaks, a blank page, a cover page, an envelope or label sheets; at is a paragraph or table id (insert after it), {id, offset}, or "start"/"end", and breaks are refused inside table cells.
            Use read_document what=comments to get ids like c:3 before manage_comments reply, edit, resolve, unresolve or delete; add takes one target (paragraph id with optional start/end or match, a table id needs row and column) and the text; replies and resolve act on the whole thread. manage_revisions track_on and track_off switch change tracking; while on, insert_paragraphs, delete_paragraphs, set_table_cell, edit_text, replace_text and replace_paragraph are recorded as tracked changes; accept and reject default to every change, narrowed by targets, revision_ids (like r:4), author and types.
            set_document_settings changes title, subject, author, keywords, description, category, company, the editing restriction (none, read_only, comments_only, tracked_changes_only; no password), default language, default tab stop in cm and update-fields-on-open; after read_only or comments_only every other writing tool is refused until it is set back to none.
            """;
    }
}
